        "original_id": "459cc91b-6768-5df1-870c-a3190b151be0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Schuyler, A. E. Housman, John Ashbery, Kenneth Koch\n- Organizations: Locus Solus\n- Works: A Shropshire Lad, On Wenlock Edge\n- Roles: poets, editor, classical scholar\n\nFacts:\n- A. E. Housman, born Alfred Edward Housman, was an English classical scholar and poet who lived from 26 March 1859 to 30 April 1936.\n- A. E. Housman was best known to the general public for his 1896 poetry collection A Shropshire Lad.\n- On Wenlock Edge is a song cycle that sets six poems from A. E. Housman's 1896 collection A Shropshire Lad.\n- James Marcus Schuyler was an American poet who lived from November 9, 1923 to April 12, 1991.\n- Locus Solus was edited by the poets John Ashbery, Kenneth Koch, and James Schuyler.\n- John Ashbery, Kenneth Koch, and James Schuyler each contributed to all four issues of Locus Solus.",
